--- body ---
## Context

Split from ticket 0693 by the raid's Imagine phase (2026-09-06). This is
**not** a direct author request: neither ticket 0686 nor the author's
2026-09-06 remarks ask for a notification channel. It is motivated by
ecosystem convention -- most widely-adopted Zotero plugins surface
background-task feedback through a transient, non-blocking toast rather
than requiring the user to keep a dialog open. That argument holds up, but
it is this ticket's own synthesis, not a ratified decision, and it adds
new accessibility surface (screen-reader announcement of transient toasts,
timing, dismissal) on top of ticket 0686's already-open, still-unverified
accessibility items. Get a quick author nod before building this -- it is
cheap to ask and the alternative is stacking unverified a11y surface on
unverified a11y surface.

## Mechanism

Use **`Zotero.ProgressWindow`** (Zotero's own bundled global) directly,
not `zotero-plugin-toolkit`. This plugin has zero build tooling -- no
`package.json`, no bundler; `bootstrap.js`/`scheduler.js` load raw via
`Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript`. Pulling in `zotero-plugin-toolkit`
would mean introducing a bundler for the first time solely to get a toast.
`Zotero.ProgressWindow` needs no new dependency and no build step, and is
the same primitive the toolkit wraps.

## Design

One completion/exceptions toast, gated on the sweep having actually
processed something -- diff `state.completed`/`state.failed` before and
after the `await sitter.sweep()` call (mirroring the existing
`lastCompleted`/`completionBlinkUntil` diffing pattern already in
bootstrap.js), and skip the toast entirely on an empty/idle sweep. The
sweep wrapper reschedules on a fixed 30s timer for the life of the
plugin -- it is not a bounded "overnight sweep" -- so a toast fired
unconditionally on every call would repeat every 30 seconds forever once
the library is caught up: strictly worse than the "dozens of toasts per
run" this ticket already set out to avoid.

No separate "job start" toast: it cannot be worded per-document (a sweep
call can touch zero, one, or many files, so there is no single `<title>`
to name "at sweep start"), and it is redundant with the toolbar's own
already-shipped ambient indicators (spinning glyph while a file is
active, opacity pulse during census).

Text for the failure count depends on `state.failed`, which ticket 0699
(open, reopened, zero acceptance boxes checked) documents as currently
both over- and under-reporting. Land this ticket after 0699, or scope
its first cut to a completion-only toast ("N fichiers indexes") and defer
the failure-inclusive wording until 0699's fix lands.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Toasts use `Zotero.ProgressWindow`; no new dependency added.
- [x] Author has confirmed this ticket should proceed (recorded in the log).
- [ ] The toast fires only when a sweep call actually processed
      candidates (completed/failed count changed), never on a bare timer
      tick with nothing to report.
- [ ] No per-document or per-sweep-start toast; only a completion/
      exceptions toast.
- [ ] Toast text uses only the vocabulary from ticket 0691 -- no internal
      jargon -- and the failure count it displays is the one 0699 fixes,
      not the pre-fix count.
